Integrating the Registry into the Portfolio Controller
The Portfolio Controller instantiates a CSymbolRegistry object, initializes it from the universe file, and exposes per-symbol lot limits through the shared global variable channel. These limits are derived from actual contract specifications — tick size, tick value, volume step — combined with a fixed nominal stop distance used as a placeholder rather than a calibrated risk distance (see Design Decisions below).
The registry instance is owned by the Portfolio Controller. Instrument Agents do not instantiate their own copy of the controller's registry — each agent maintains a smaller, self-contained registry scoped to its own symbol, described below. This design ensures that contract specification queries happen in one place at a controlled frequency for the controller's universe, rather than being scattered across every agent's tick handler.
//+------------------------------------------------------------------+
//|                                    PortfolioController_v2.mq5    |
//|         Portfolio Controller with symbol registry integration    |
//+------------------------------------------------------------------+
#property
copyright
"Institutional Portfolio Series"
#property
version
"2.00"
#property
